  "theoretical_novelty": "This research introduces a novel theoretical framework that integrates computational linguistics and cultural psychology to understand the mechanisms behind unsafe outputs in multilingual contexts. By identifying linguistic and cultural factors as moderators of LLM behavior, it advances knowledge on how these elements influence model outputs, thereby providing a deeper understanding of safety alignment across diverse languages.",
  "methodological_novelty": "The development of the XSafety benchmark represents a significant methodological advancement, as it systematically evaluates 14 distinct safety issues across ten languages, focusing specifically on non-English queries. This mixed-methods approach combines quantitative metrics with qualitative analyses, allowing for a comprehensive assessment of LLM safety that has not been previously achieved.",
  "practical_translational_novelty": "The findings from this research will have practical implications for the deployment of LLMs in multilingual environments, enhancing their safety and controllability in sensitive applications. By providing insights into the internal representations of LLMs, the study will inform the design of safer AI systems that are better aligned with cultural and linguistic nuances, thus contributing to responsible AI development."
}

